{"step_index":42,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T22:56:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T17:56:26-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T17:56:29-05:00\nThe search for \"\"GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK\" OR \"CYBERLEEK\" \"GTA6\"\" returned the following summary:\nThis query references a major leak involving **Grand Theft Auto VI (GTA 6)** associated with an online persona or group named **Cyberleek**[1]. \n\n### Key Details Surrounding the Leak:\n* **The Build:** Cyberleek circulated a torrent containing a near-complete developer build of *Grand Theft Auto VI* (labeled as an Xbox Series build, patch #2, version `v01.002.001` / `v1.0.2.1`, dated mid-November 2026)[1]. \n* **The Executable (.exe):** Initially, the large data leak withheld the main executable file (`.exe`), which is required to actually initialize the game[2]. Cyberleek tied the release of the `.exe` to a countdown timer (ending November 23, 2026) and a cryptocurrency market cap milestone[3][4]. \n* **The Release:** True to their word, Cyberleek published the `.exe` file alongside specific SHA-256 cryptographic hashes to verify its authenticity[5][4]. \n* **Impact on PC Port / Emulation Communities:** Because the Xbox Series consoles share a close architectural foundation with Windows, the release of this executable file immediately energized open-source reverse-engineering, recompilation, and emulation projects (such as PC port efforts like *Leonida*)[6][7][8]. \n* **Intentions and Response:** Cyberleek framed the leak as an anti-consumer statement directed at Take-Two Interactive and Rockstar Games regarding the lack of a native PC release date, while taunting ongoing corporate and legal takedown efforts[9][10][4]. \n\n*Note: While this development is a significant milestone for reverse-engineering and emulation enthusiasts, security experts and developers have cautioned that end-users cannot simply download and smoothly play a finished version of GTA 6 on PC, as extensive translation of shaders, memory management, and bug-fixing are still required by developers[11][9].*\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGP-kKFXVegUmGqdTUaKLnyZYMPBecm8pHerjCRmkVQ7FxFyLbwPyAsTVnm5g4Tn8bZwdkDTrGnDpX4YSgwSW9zskH1WBJi2CjWmJW4FQeLgba1CYs3qXQv1x_IsfRhvCUfdWenW6UGaMgnPdeZkFdDX-HnlG_KkJuvGf9B7O-cCcAEyLf7XMF4nG7qUcwdQ7HY-YK5rB4S)\n[2] [80.lv](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEPtQlmdpD4aqlCq6WqroQfhaO0z3avVEpB4NAXEySZBE2q_l-TZyp10Nt3JpfBvywdEjqPqRUnszk6g2tOLah4oo_PYG3ymyHkyUOo7d-5jlHJ57oic5gq1opFvu4TYUtBz__rP3_ULij-X6EQ4Nq4e_VE9UQcAHmwyEyvRo_0SEP2t1pnUQUsIg==)\n[3] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHQKRPhE90NFftBqH2F43EttEk3yp2i1d1kzvqwP5PCD_v0oHx6M_vMMAzf9ijnUoCweS5CNho7dBctmHT976YMomWDmsSnu_G8CRY8hgvckkQRF7ReFVWJ1eDdJF5E65PcgwCFzyfnpPVPVnJavIAFB9H8MS9DAdg77HNKdvFFM_kajSsHDvDlw-G1MiNavAhP0CzBGegyfP3EO9PxH1I=)\n[4] [pcgamer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrUFBrp3-lYKIH492XBY_yXD7lusqRRlhKDYRkFhTf9bVGwdNouxkhYcncCUijVqtOOHO_GgzW2Bey26U8g_3KbHFZdKjyKGs2WLJwTorAsX-ChizwLl_gYmEOsknwjqzUAlYyQ02klIT1mtcWJ8783QCxCst45JCLa7LisxHJsGlEOjMYZeZv_yM_TQ5pKasLmo5MyLdtbpZ7YIXXcMRNKijQHBe8_wUX-3APPPzBteflF_H3jJwcoCjlfLBgkjhM020hN7Qk38ho-hroTZwCluwTkzpJzhpH27xGF8_x_GfeDM5X9jof6NI9)\n[5] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGTQJlsTZ18Fcs0SBvYbbrbUwWsr4grIu8vvAycHhFl3ww8WzSGx-00BEPA8CltcEkO5iTFSf5eZLDKqbAt3XucEZu8lCqGa7LTgR4z1HeNLwM_4G5vydKjkEmCBOlwUg_3oysKfIWYD-bXAUt8_IdRNP1lClX48AouFjcS9neW95bCDgnW4pJ16PQgKlfen58NOfaTQlNkWtVsoi8hAuwCTWsZeotZ)\n[6] [pcgamer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrUFBrp3-lYKIH492XBY_yXD7lusqRRlhKDYRkFhTf9bVGwdNouxkhYcncCUijVqtOOHO_GgzW2Bey26U8g_3KbHFZdKjyKGs2WLJwTorAsX-ChizwLl_gYmEOsknwjqzUAlYyQ02klIT1mtcWJ8783QCxCst45JCLa7LisxHJsGlEOjMYZeZv_yM_TQ5pKasLmo5MyLdtbpZ7Y