{"step_index":44,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T22:56:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T17:56:33-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T17:56:36-05:00\nThe search for \"\"GTA 6\" \"CYBERLEEK\" missions OR \"mission list\" OR \"mission flow\" OR \"story000\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe association between **\"Cyberleek\"** and internal development assets like **`story000`**, mission flows, or specific mission lists traces back to major security breaches and data dumps connected to *Grand Theft Auto VI*[1][2]. \n\n### 1. What is \"Cyberleek\"?\n\"Cyberleek\" is the moniker associated with a high-profile leaker (or group) tied to circulating deep development assets, gameplay footage, and internal files regarding *GTA 6*[1][2]. While initial massive leaks hit the web years prior, Cyberleek made headlines around the game's launch window by releasing extensive unedited gameplay, debug information, and internal build components (such as executable files and string data from leaked Xbox/debug developer builds)[2][3].\n\n### 2. Mission Flows, `story000`, and Internal Nomenclature\nIn Rockstar Games' proprietary RAGE engine development structure, internal mission scripts and debug strings are typically categorized systematically:\n* **`story000` / Prologue files:** In leaked debugging nomenclature, text strings, global states, and master flow scripts often begin with `story000` or foundational index tags to dictate the initialization of the game's script logic, character switching parameters, and cutscene triggers.\n* **Mission Flow & Lists:** Leaked internal debugging trees and development text assets gave data-miners an early look at how chapters transition. In these developer documents, missions are categorized by internal codenames before receiving final retail titles. \n\n### 3. Leaks vs. The Final Release\nWhile early data-miners combed through Cyberleek's dumps looking for mission flow lines, debug names, and placeholder scripts (`story000`, etc.), the actual game launched with a structured campaign consisting of roughly 91 main story missions spanning 5 distinct chapters featuring protagonists Jason and Lucia[4]:\n* **Chapter 1:** *Just Like Paradise* (Leonida Keys / Prologue setup, ending with missions like *Tourist Trap*)[5][6]\n* **Chapter 2:** *Paradise Lost* (Port Gellhorn)[7]\n* **Chapters 3–5:** Moving into the broader Vice City criminal underworld and epilogue sequences[4][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [mmoexp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHNX7TtsWLQnK8jPacTJB6qX3GRsgslo5nnhRZBB7LLU0escjN4jMagTpZxZWUVCMt5asjaujaWuPailDRBWNKe_t2DShVRnjTc-0el_TJ2WGiCokhgc22ZyByEh_lwQTI9k1x60hE-Tb9xnSwsk95cPNaC3HeCHY4tU9EFSJb8FQd1zTOoEmQYN0ZF7q8JxPqoGkyJjE5CsZvJJ34dSTzQJN0i)\n[2] [gamesindustry.biz](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE6pCr5rWPTCjyQyk1-4510ScFeLoinNMwNYEZ4MxKg1n3xAZZ5EkNCZHE4lCEwTRnGjDc28VF9rivuV9kJvrvc5-k3TrOAreDePK9m0wt8d8oIyG6xyQnYpofAeMNcQFzs5djzuvNqS4nZD_cn-t5rGlqi05Z1ffUcf6v_XD7vlZgIqY7p9eI7swKxzZIu2Qy04czHmdsD5jA=)\n[3] [ign.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFyAdPIspshzGdRgr73ZK6KCl4cmvrrNKajY3AN8fKOWJQ1Y69KX88McOkycnnt7-SL0VMavpNmTCwmHt34waIs4tCynvWKagTUGQik9ACUy_Djrfp6CCfZVwKUFD_euOpLaC7wuTJ6wEl4tYo51wOJBpKTaZjknVVq-SuZGylZsL1CDS1bbrMWbows_ClSi8OEACyj12cYuBaKDcL6RxeKXvEnkkFOfXQc_gr1qUeZ8u8a0aM3LdfesQK7wewZKxHDnBFt_M4UHTjLkg8VsvlmV_cCzQgBEM5_)\n[4] [g2a.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFA41dohDteKPCpua_Rq_40-_osaiOzAcm8jIi-mW_cx8QPsA50d4twBNs5LcqHHE8FdcFP6Ybjp01UwDeWTZUf1Oky_7iv2V0NC7pNkHbGcq_no5epJnOiwxcr0Txi6h86-YB570f837LbbBe0Ao2Acsud6kiq6RJT)\n[5] [pcgamer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHIxcBxv65IRW-ecqII4G1Qn5TemAx-F_C5pAT4EBW7Hw53U5IbTIwQv4gJtDzRWKI7PpvOTCpFtsiVtNX0ZE_Bw2-13cK4FDQccOMHt61oTyUvkGhSHoIF_ew7yZSZB6QY2s2Rcy6xou5l748vKi_VQHVcPp56uU=)\n[6] [gamesradar.com](ht