{"step_index":54,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T22:57:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T17:57:01-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T17:57:05-05:00\nThe search for \"\"struct RpfHeader\" OR \"struct rpf_header\" OR \"RPF8\" header struct github\" returned the following summary:\nIf you are looking for GitHub repositories, documentation, or code snippets defining the **RAGE Package File (RPF)** header structure (used across Rockstar Games titles like *GTA V*, *Red Dead Redemption 2*, etc.)[1][2], implementations typically look like this:\n\n### 1. Typical C / C++ or Rust Header Layout (`RPF7` / `RPF8`)\n\nIn open-source tooling (such as CodeWalker[3], community documentation[2], or Rust libraries like `rpf-archive`[1]), the root header layout maps conceptually to a structure like the following:\n\n```c\nstruct RpfHeader {\n    uint32_t magic;           // \"RPF7\" (0x37465052) or \"RPF8\" (0x38465052)\n    uint32_t entryCount;      // Total number of file and directory entries\n    uint32_t namesLength;     // Size of the string blob for file/dir names (absent/0 in some RPF8 implementations)\n    uint32_t encryptionType;  // 0 = None, OPEN (0x4E45504F), AES, or NG\n};\n```[4][2]\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key GitHub Repositories & References\n\nTo inspect exact struct definitions, parsing routines, and decryption logic on GitHub, look into these prominent open-source projects:\n\n* **[Bobrokus/rpf7-docs](https://github.com/Bobrokus/rpf7-docs)** – Clean, breakdown documentation mapping out the exact header offsets, entry counts, and encryption type enums for `RPF7`[2].\n* **[dexyfex/CodeWalker](https://github.com/dexyfex/CodeWalker)** – The primary C# open-source reference for Rockstar's RAGE engine files. Check its `RpfFile.cs` implementation for the most authoritative parsing of header blocks across `RPF2` through `RPF8`[3].\n* **[wjy000/gtav-enhanced-rpf](https://github.com/wjy000/gtav-enhanced-rpf)** – Python tooling focusing on newer Gen9/Enhanced RPF structures and block ciphers[5].\n* **[zeozeozeo/rpf7](https://github.com/zeozeozeo/rpf7)** or similar crates under the **`rpf-archive`** ecosystem – Rust implementations parsing RPF headers, TOC entries, and resource flags (`RSC7`)[1][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGnNYDyk56IPpGPtgDbctAWjMXUo00jzVHkPLWB3Pw5hU63oMawtCbm2hkiytBJP1y-cR3KIXhNGLghCXWq7VyAlOEIsCwM28oMH6ZYtvLunH5GF5Z0MjYj)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE89-WdumCTF83P8xtRQgi_uwEXWgGhYtHa_NFv1Bgz3XE2wyFi1EJFIACJ5l86B8K08_iqrjXt1yIGeHb8KGJ4IiBSIf31EKVNjiRlJdHutxut7p3EFW5lIhW4)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFnkOrVnu3RwbLiqZ9WIj8n6ZqIv0mrHgZ81UyIe7hrEVZcb9yCEJLLcWAnmNl-C1m4GWnfxXeqc7oVDM8dxOLnbfybLnz_nHEAhbdEvJhIwpMICoeA6vtNurF_mmGcerhvNWbgxPC3h9Slrf1aP2BG0OpRLZrENuJiBjc-lxzRX4I=)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFnkOrVnu3RwbLiqZ9WIj8n6ZqIv0mrHgZ81UyIe7hrEVZcb9yCEJLLcWAnmNl-C1m4GWnfxXeqc7oVDM8dxOLnbfybLnz_nHEAhbdEvJhIwpMICoeA6vtNurF_mmGcerhvNWbgxPC3h9Slrf1aP2BG0OpRLZrENuJiBjc-lxzRX4I=)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHYXkK5EJKB8Q2t_-FPgeVrLH57Q1sZILB403o5MpNiQPa2ZTiMsXPOOuJB-4khDGHuplAhTlcZtMEm4z3_omeR_-LKE__TLkTkZzMppBx07-t3tHADQINBsEnD8WK7LqiX)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrTeUZKOkyUCn7s4ltXmhMSKn2b5ylu-H8uePvusF6R72ED4OxkcNAXlLUZueVdv7vRnqv4YfPJdMGc__T0Dl_TPB2z3x1dGLjcvV3afF8WyyMvc9lb5o=)"}
