{"step_index":90,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T22:58:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T17:58:38-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T17:58:41-05:00\nThe search for \"\"Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise\" \"Chapter 2: Paradise Lost\" all missions list\" returned the following summary:\nHere is the complete mission list for **Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise** and **Chapter 2: Paradise Lost** in *Grand Theft Auto VI*[1]. \n\n---\n\n### **Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise**\n*Setting: Leonida Keys / Key Lento (Focuses heavily on Jason working local smuggling/odd jobs while Lucia is initially in prison, leading up to her release and their life together in the Keys)[2][3][4].*\n\n1. **Prologue** (Lucia meets with her prison counselor)[5]\n2. **Gone Fishing** (Jason and Donnie skim some bricks off a shipment)[5][6]\n3. **Gear Up** (Jason picks up a longarm/gear for Brian)[5][6]\n4. **Just a Scratch** (Jason gets the Ganado repaired and painted)[5][6]\n5. **Lab Fees** (Jason collects Brian's rent at the Moonstone Boutique)[5][6]\n6. **Unwanted Attention** (Cal and Jason head to Hamlet)[5]\n7. **Pipework** (Jason handles some DIY tasks)[5]\n8. **Hey Arnold!** (Brian, Jason, and Cal track down a broker)[5]\n9. **Island Dreams** (Jason goes diving)[5]\n10. **Feng Shui** (Jason and Cal move furniture)[5]\n11. **Coming Home** (Lucia is released and reunites with Jason)[5][4]\n12. **Clean Up After Donnie** (Jason retrieves a package near Hamlet)[5][3]\n13. **Buck Me** (Jason and Lucia do some banking)[5]\n14. **Down to Earth** (Jason and Lucia do a smuggling run from the marina)[5][3]\n15. **Clear Skies** (Jason and Donnie deal with local bikers in Southwind)[5][3]\n16. **Day Release** (Mattia, Jason, and Lucia have a night out starting at the Rusty Anchor)[5][3]\n17. **Swamped** (Jason, Brian, and Lorrie meet the Kingfishers)[5][3]\n18. **Don Gone** (Clearing out Donnie's trailer on Brian's orders)[3]\n19. **Recalibration** (Jason and Lucia help Cal through a rough patch)[3]\n20. **Tourist Trap** (Accepting Mattia's pickup job offer)[3]\n21. **Home Sweet Home** (Dealing with the fallout of recent events)[3]\n22. **Discharge Time** (Checking in on Jason after the chapter's climax)[3]\n*(Note: Depending on platform tracking or optional checklist thresholds, some platform indices tally up to 23–25 total story entries with introductory tasks[7][6][4]).*\n\n---\n\n### **Chapter 2: Paradise Lost**\n*Setting: Port Gellhorn & Kelly County (Jason is recovering from injuries while Lucia carries out local car thefts, small robberies, and odd jobs laying low before setting sights on Vice City)[8][3][9].*\n\n1. **What's in the Bag?**[8][10]\n2. **Overnight Charges**[8][10]\n3. **Take Care of Jason**[10]\n4. **Just Moved In**[8][10]\n5. **Girl's Trip**[10]\n6. **Moses**[10]\n7. **New Look**[10]\n8. **How Do I Look?**[10]\n9. **Behind on Payments**[10]\n10. **Ambulance Chaser**[10]\n11. **Painkiller Supplier**[10]\n12. **Daily Driver**[10]\n13. **Pick Up A Gun**[10]\n14. **Slam Dunk**[10]\n15. **Breakfast Run**[10]\n16. **Coffee Break** *(Unlocks manual character switching between Jason and Lucia)*[7][10]\n17. **Hit Avery Pawn**[10]\n18. **Hit Kingpin Bowling**[10]\n19. **Impounded Vehicle**[10]\n20. **Afternoon Delight**[10]\n21. **Prepare for Vice City**[10]\n22. **Checking Out** *(Transition mission leading into Chapter 3: Tits, Ass, Drug Money)*[2][10]\n\nSources:\n[1] [space4games.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGW1Wf7706UwSc_fwBH2cKzs4HtU-ZkfjmDXpJzFF_ZPAtS4GBlE7boLu1Xva4KCKe0pHmQX-sFFBwd4KpHvRv45nFzDLpy8AF3657uQqT4e_-KcRPDJbrP-w1NTz2QFRYrzQ3Qh1_W9QhnEnterbFieRxRomL0RY8ElIloJ0vw-Dz3gLPQ)\n[2] [gamesradar.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHg_V3ecKHMjqkWzNeLTLc3lHNfwZNJ_hdLkptfwtJCXAVGomTEydK2kgDOp2clOAmVF5RlYJWqMTp8pbkq8ZzeAvKc3a2pmjxvqSdV5sJWnHWRdQYAdPXLwRpPiR39TOkDVrJQSnkeR430yG95mfefuaTL0Y9Any-uHUc=)\n[3] [skycoach.gg](https://vert